+@captain @conformance
+Feature: Empty-edit commit removes the item without a re-entrant render
+
+  A real browser holds the edit input element focused inside the item being
+  edited. When the user commits an edit whose text is empty, the app removes
+  that item; removing the item detaches the focused edit input and fires a blur.
+  The app's blur handler must not re-enter the destroy or render path, because
+  re-entering removes an already-detached node and throws a "removeChild" error
+  ("The node to be removed is no longer a child of this node. Perhaps it was
+  moved in a 'blur' event handler?"). The in-harness DOM does not fire the
+  re-entrant blur, so this product defect is pinned by a source-level check on
+  the edit-commit and destroy path.
+
+  Scenario: Empty-edit commit removes the item without a re-entrant render
+    Given the implementation directories from RIGGING.md
+    When the empty-edit-removal conformance check inspects the edit-commit and destroy path
+    Then committing an empty edit removes the item without re-entering the render path or throwing a removeChild error
